          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1353a53e6aa0343f3daa26fe62ed925421ffbf934b2b6c3288ebefe4d17dd64d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e7db2dc235b8439caf7be2cbba67c87e",
      "statement": "CreateFullPose emits one position and one rotation channel per bone in skeleton depth-first order so that element index equals bone index, which is what lets every FK loop and every consumer index a bone directly without a lookup.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Pose/PoseLayout.cs#L152-L189",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f47ba50b69b2ec832f82cae34f771096a598afd798b61d84957a549a3e6440ef:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Tests/Editor/PoseLayoutTests.cs#L221-L265",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:722003cb8e2605dcdeac95ec705332672a1495c0562325b83326647de32d14af:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8ba0b77aa5f54e3a827ab757beab4423",
      "statement": "PoseBuffer.Lerp applies a different rule per section: positions, scales and velocities interpolate componentwise, quaternion rotations are hemisphere-corrected before lerp and renormalisation, booleans step at the halfway point rather than blending, and any extra tail section falls back to linear because it has no per-kind rule.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Pose/PoseBuffer.cs#L71-L141",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3d9078f5fde4c3a78399bcdee25260f8b262326224c52ab7a6da23b73fb9644e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Tests/Editor/PoseBufferTests.cs#L185-L238",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b610bdad53cd9ffd016f8782c56ed38cccda550724130ba8ed14b9cd1fe39b27:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_364843c3d7974602a70b3d8c957bcc68",
      "statement": "PoseLayoutBuilder is the single authoritative motion-matching pose layout, built through by both PoseSet and MotionSynthesisComponent over the same skeleton so the cache hands them one instance and frames can be copied between them.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Pose/PoseLayoutBuilder.cs#L6-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6ceb651b43e0ee59775b46449bbebb4026d4b3603756b9a55d965c773d25dcf2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_726cfeb0dff040499cfe5093b9716596",
      "statement": "The contact host bone for each side must be a pure function of the skeleton's bone names and never of the skeleton's source, because otherwise the database side and the runtime side would pick different bones for the same rig, producing different channel identities and therefore different layout hashes and a failing CopyFrom.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Pose/PoseLayoutBuilder.cs#L6-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6ceb651b43e0ee59775b46449bbebb4026d4b3603756b9a55d965c773d25dcf2:"
        },
        {
