          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8fe44280a669d1d3da5014e293ab7efd139edb277043e5cc6a98fdbb1784cf08:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_53a5a4ba956d496c9f8689b281cb61dc",
      "statement": "ChannelSpace is descriptive metadata folded into the content hash and is never enforced: every channel PoseLayoutBuilder creates is declared ParentLocal including bone 0's, which by the storage convention actually holds world position and rotation, so bone-0-is-world is a convention upheld by callers rather than something the layout expresses.",
